1: # Plan 6: command-owned automasking preparation and cavity caches
2: 
3: Reviewed by fresh preparation/transaction and cache/geometry CLI reviewers;
4: findings and dispositions below are incorporated before implementation.
5: The prepared MASK gate is complete; this closes the next native
6: capability dependency before generic host adoption.
7: 
8: ## Current seams
9: 
10: - PreparedBrushScalars includes common properties and kernel uniforms only.
11:   Executor-owned cavity/view-normal settings are absent from both that set and
12:   Brush::builtinPropDescriptorSpan, although they are reflected native members.
13: - Mesh/grid prepared admission rejects brush.automask_cavity wholesale. Removing
14:   the guard alone would miss later-command enable, topology preparation and cache
15:   separation. Both raw executors cache one remapped factor per vertex/stroke.
16: - Mesh cavity needs ring1 ensured before freezing. Command overrides must be
17:   validated before any cache, attribute, topology, store or undo mutation.
18: - The frozen contract requires command-independent stroke-static cavity and
19:   reflected geometric viewDir on the future generic symmetry path. Existing raw
20:   view-normal policy pins a camera ray; retain it for legacy execution. This slice
21:   prepares the static settings; generic per-image viewDir adoption remains in the
22:   host consumer task and must use the frozen contract's independent expectations.
23: 
24: ## Implementation
25: 
26: 1. Add an explicit executor-owned static scalar catalogue for automask_cavity,
27:    cavity_factor, cavity_blur_steps, cavity_inverted, cavity_use_curve,
28:    automask_view_normal, cull_backfaces, view_normal_limit, view_normal_falloff.
29:    Add these authoritative native members to builtin descriptors with dynamics
30:    disabled. The catalogue is engine-owned, separate from DSL kernel manifests.
31:    Prepare this fixed set for every prepared command, using native member values
32:    unless the command supplies an exact typed override. Include matching values
33:    in scoped restoration, without publishing persistent property declarations or
34:    default slots merely for these executor settings. Reject device stacks on this
35:    static set, unknown IDs, type mismatch and nonfinite float values. Retain full
36:    finite FLOAT32 domains and signed INT32 transport; blur must be nonnegative and
37:    less than INT32_MAX to make the BFS depth increment defined. Validate before
38:    mutation, including a disabled cavity configuration with malformed parameters.
39: 2. Add optional command-owned cavity LUT payload with exact 256 finite FLOAT32
40:    samples. Omitted payload inherits the Brush LUT; explicit identity LUT replaces
41:    it. Copy into the prepared command candidate, never retain caller pointers.
42:    Add checked public replacement/removal transport and generated bindings using
43:    established Vector<float> transport. A failed upload preserves the previous
44:    command. Include the LUT in working-state restoration on every exit. Raw paths
45:    explicitly reject command LUT overrides, including zero-dab automatic fallback.
46: 3. Candidate preparation resolves each command's full cavity configuration before
47:    spatial selection. Union the requirement for enabled positive-radius commands.
48:    After complete preflight and a nonempty region, ensure mesh ring1 before freeze
49:    even when only a later command enables cavity. Do not change unrelated prepared
50:    guards (dyntopo, anchored/unbounded, general attributes, host stages, previews).
51: 4. Prepared execution gets executor-owned transient cavity cache entries keyed by
52:    exact full configuration (blur, factor, inversion, use-curve and complete LUT),
53:    current mesh/domain identity, stroke transaction and topology generation.
54:    Hashes may accelerate lookup but cannot replace equality checks. Cache sparse
55:    per-vertex factors per entry, frozen at that configuration's first contact.
56:    BeginStep/attach/rebuild retires entries; mesh topology changes retire stale
57:    entries. Ordinary coordinate deformation does not invalidate first-contact
58:    values within a stroke: that preserves the existing cavity contract. Filling
59:    occurs serially before parallel kernels; references remain stable during the
60:    kernel. Identical configurations share work, different configurations never
61:    share a remapped factor. Cache no-op/miss/rejected commands cannot publish data.
62: 5. Preserve legacy raw cavity execution and cache policy when the generic/prepared
63:    path is not used. Introduce a scoped prepared execution context to select the
64:    new cache inside shared exec/execStage without leaking into subsequent raw dabs.
65:    Keep live view-normal evaluation and camera data outside cavity cache identity.
66:    Cache growth is bounded by distinct static configurations in the stroke; tests
67:    cover reuse, reset and changed configurations. No persistent cache serialization.
68: 
69: ## Acceptance
70: 
71: - Read-only candidate tests for authoritative static bool/int/float sources,
72:   independent command overrides, absent properties, invalid/stale inputs, static
73:   dynamics rejection and exact working/LUT restoration. Keep failed late commands
74:   atomic before ring1 preparation, allocation, undo capture and counters.
75: - Independent cavity oracle using cavityRawT/cavityRemap on the configuration's
76:   first-contact geometry; test different blur/factor/inversion/LUT, later-command
77:   enable, larger secondary radius, newly reached vertices, same-config reuse,
78:   changed stroke/topology/domain identity, and no accidental per-dab recomputation.
79: - Actual mesh live/CSR and grid immediate/deferred execution; standalone/program,
80:   Python transport, input batches, mask+draw+smooth, exact undo/cancel and subsequent
81:   raw/prepared strokes. Default-off cavity remains identical to prior gate outputs.
82: - Snapshot cache payload/evaluation counts in tests to prove configuration
83:   separation and warm reuse. Test failed LUT replacement/removal, caller mutation,
84:   inherited vs explicit identity, cold upload and required prepared policy.
85: - Extend the safe headed harness with actual cavity settings and demonstrate a
86:   measurable difference from cavity off. Native/Python builds, generated bindings,
87:   applicable regression matrix, installed package and provenance smoke.
88: 
89: This gate does not claim generic UI, owner resolution in the modal operator,
90: viewDir symmetry adoption or Plan 6 completion. Those remain explicit next tasks.
91: 
92: ## Review corrections and decisions — 2026-09-18
93: 
94: - Dedicated catalogue pass: supply explicit temporary ScalarDeclaration domains
95:   to prepareValue, with dynamic=false, authoritative native addressing and no
96:   insertion into declarations_. Validate existing property identity/type/schema/
97:   stacks but ignore property value/getter/range for the static native value.
98:   Catalogue entries named by DSL manifests must exactly match type/static/range
99:   policy; reject conflicts and prepare the target once. Normal kernel processing
100:   must not republish a catalogue declaration.
101: - Typed command transport already exists outside the first review packet:
102:   BrushProgram_setScalarChecked in mesh_stroke_batch_c_api.cc and Python
103:   set_command_scalar in brush_properties.py. Retain/test that checked float64
104:   transport for BOOL, signed INT32 and FLOAT32; do not add a competing scalar API.
105:   Add bound LUT methods with an explicit native C seam if reflection proves unable
106:   to call them, as required by the prior command-stack transport experience.
107: - Resolve/copy all 256 LUT entries for every stage before execution, including
108:   inheritance and disabled configurations. Validate public raw mutations again
109:   at preparation. Apply each stage's complete LUT, even when it inherited, so a
110:   preceding override cannot leak. Removal resumes inheritance on next preparation.
111: - Standalone retains its existing common-scalar publication behavior (accepted
112:   misses/zero calls included). Protect only the new executor-owned settings/LUT
113:   with a dedicated scope before first working write; program scope additionally
114:   restores all prepared working values as before. Rejected candidates publish no
115:   declarations or persistent/executor/mesh allocation; scratch allocation is allowed.
116: - First contact means a vertex inside the executing command's spherical radius
117:   (strict normalized distance <1) immediately before that command's kernel. The
118:   larger shared program leaf union does not establish contact for a smaller
119:   command. BFS may read neighbors outside the support without caching them.
120:   Accepted positive-radius zero-strength/texture/mask-effect stages may cache
121:   those in-support vertices; there is no general promise to detect every no-op.
122:   Zero radius, no in-support vertices and rejected preflight cannot fill entries.
123: - For stale ring1 on an already frozen mesh, thaw after complete validation and
124:   nonempty selection, ensure ring1, then apply the program's freeze/live policy.
125:   A prepared cavity stage requires valid ring1 and never silently bypasses cavity.
126: - Reuse one executor-owned CavityScratch across entries. Warm hits do no BFS and
127:   no capacity-sized scratch initialization. Measure configuration-vertex payload
128:   and evaluation counts. No eviction/recomputation from changed geometry is allowed
129:   within a transaction. beginStep retires cache even if mesh strokeGen repeats.
130: - Oracle geometry is captured immediately before the cache fill: current co/no
131:   as supplied by the chosen immediate/deferred normal policy. Test A -> deform
132:   -> B -> A, newly entered support, each key field and in-place LUT mutation.
133:   Compare each policy against its own independent oracle, not assumed parity
134:   between policies with different normal refresh cadence.
135: 
136: Implementation seam checks: non-accumulating contact uses the same derived base
137: coordinate as its AccumOrig vertex iterator (cavity's BFS still samples live
138: geometry). Kernels evaluate automasks even when strength() returns zero, so every
139: visited vertex needs a valid factor address. Keep a reusable active factor column
140: for the current stage, set outside-support visited vertices to identity, and copy
141: cached in-support factors into it. Cache entries store only contacted vertex/value
142: pairs; the stage column's materialized pages are separate reusable scratch.
